error[SC0307]: the declarations of `f` disagree about nullability
   ╭─[ an_unprototyped_declaration_disagrees_about_a_return.c:2:7 ]
   │
 1 │ int *f();
   │      ┬  
   │      ╰── the first declaration says nothing
 2 │ int * _Nonnull f(void);
   │       ────┬───  
   │           ╰───── one declaration says `_Nonnull` here
───╯
  = note: every declaration of a function has to agree about its nullability specifiers, because each of them is a promise to the function's callers
